- Write an encryption program that reads from cin and writes the encoded
character to cout. You might use this simple encryption scheme: the encrypted
form of character c is c^key[i], where key is a string passed as a command-line
argument. The program uses the characters in key in a cyclic manner until all
the input has been read. Re-encrypting encoded text with the same key produces
the original text. If no kye (or a null string) is passed, then no encryption is
done.
